From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:27:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx362: add the vendor's 16:9 and 2x2-binned
 modes

The driver only knew the full 4032x3032 array at 30 fps, so every consumer
debayered 12 MP to show a viewfinder and nothing above 30 fps was reachable.

Add three more resolutions from the same vendor sensor library the full mode
came from (libmmcamera_imx362.so, register tables at .data 0x57290 + k *
0x5dd0, timing from the sensor_lib_out_info_t array at 0xa9400):

  4032x2272  30 fps  16:9 crop, the source of 4K and 1080p video on Android
  2016x1512  60 fps  2x2 binned, full field of view
  2016x1136 120 fps  2x2 binned 16:9, starting at 60 fps

The binned modes' output PLL is pinned to the full mode's, so the CSI-2 link
runs at 1368 Mbps/lane in every mode. On this board the link passes through
Easel's MIPI bypass, which is configured once for that rate; CSI-2 is burst
mode, so a link faster than the data only lengthens LP time between lines.

HBLANK, VBLANK and the exposure range now follow the mode. The exposure range
must be updated even when VBLANK does not change: an exposure left longer
than the new frame made the sensor stretch every frame to fit, and 2016x1136
ran at 47 fps on the full mode's 3102-line maximum.

Also expose the SMIA test pattern, and share the driver mutex with the control
handler, since set_fmt already calls __v4l2_ctrl_*() under it.

Measured on taimen with libcamera, raw stream, 180 frames each, no sequence
gaps: 30.1, 30.1, 59.4 and 60.0 fps.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx362.c | 351 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 316 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

